.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Optional (attributes) metadata is supported for reading and creation in
MPQ v1 and v2, including MPQE. Its payload version 100 is independent of
the archive version. Enable selected arrays through options.attributes using
LIBMPQ_ATTRIBUTE_CRC32, _FILETIME, _MD5, and _PATCH_BIT
(each suffix has the same LIBMPQ_ATTRIBUTE prefix).
Zero disables generation. Any nonzero combination creates one (attributes)
file and consumes one reserved slot. Unknown attribute bits are rejected.
.PP
libmpq__archive_attributes_flags() queries header flags;
libmpq__file_attributes() returns available per-file CRC32, FILETIME,
MD5, and patch-bit values. Loading is lazy: missing or malformed metadata
does not prevent ordinary extraction. Availability flags distinguish zero
from missing values. No automatic checksum verification is performed.
.PP
libmpq__file_verify() explicitly compares requested available CRC32 and MD5
values against complete extracted contents. LIBMPQ_VERIFY_FILE_CRC32 and
LIBMPQ_VERIFY_FILE_MD5 select file checks. LIBMPQ_VERIFY_SECTOR_CRC checks
Adler-32 over decrypted packed sectors before decompression, using the
optional sector checksum table. LIBMPQ_VERIFY_ALL selects all three.
Checksum mismatches return success with the corresponding LIBMPQ_VERIFY_*
bits, a subset of the requested flags. A clear bit means matched or skipped.
Operation errors return negative codes and leave the mismatch mask zero.
File checksum requests require attributes; absence returns EXIST.
Sector-only requests do not require attributes. Missing values or sector
tables are skipped; single-unit files have no sector checksum table.
Zero mismatch bits do not imply that checksums were available.
.PP
LIBMPQ_FILE_FLAG_SECTOR_CRC enables writer-side sector Adler-32 generation for
sectorized COMPRESS and IMPLODE files, including encrypted files. It is
ignored for empty, raw, or single-unit files. The checksum table is not
encrypted and is compressed with zlib only when smaller. Generation is
opt-in and never enables implicit verification during extraction.
.PP
CRC32 and MD5 cover source bytes before compression; lossy ADPCM output
may differ. FILETIME defaults to zero and can be explicitly set through
libmpq__file_set_filetime() before file completion. Path addition does not
import filesystem timestamps. Generated patch bits are zero; patch creation
and application remain unsupported. Unused rows and the attributes entry
itself have zero values. Finalization writes the listfile, attributes,
then the completed hash and block tables.
.PP
The \fIlibmpq\fP library creates and reads MPQ archives, decrypts and
decompresses file data, and extracts files compressed with Huffman, zlib,
bzip2, SPARSE, PKWARE implosion, or the exclusive MPQ v2+ LZMA compression method.
Creation uses seekable v1 or v2 archives and
may be driven through a streaming writer or buffer/path convenience functions.
The current writer supports raw sectors, encrypted tables and payloads, generated
listfiles, zlib, bzip2 or SPARSE multi-compression, and exclusive MPQ v2+ LZMA
compression.
.PP
For MPQ v2+ creation, \fBLIBMPQ_COMPRESSION_LZMA\fP is an exclusive API
selector that serializes as method 0x12. It is not a multi-compression bit;
0x12 keeps its legacy bzip2-plus-zlib interpretation in MPQ v1 archives.
.PP
LIBMPQ_COMPRESSION_SPARSE (0x20) selects lossless zero-run compression in
v1 and v2 archives. In MPQ v2+, STANDARD allows the fixed SPARSE forms:
SPARSE alone (0x20), SPARSE with zlib (0x22), and SPARSE with bzip2 (0x30).
MPQ v1 retains normal compression-mask semantics under either policy,
allowing other valid combinations such as SPARSE with Huffman (0x21) or
PKWARE (0x28). In MPQ v2+, EXTENDED permits the broader valid lossless
SPARSE combinations. Neither policy allows SPARSE combined with WAVE ADPCM.
Extraction returns the original bytes without changing text encodings.
.PP
Writer compression defaults to STANDARD for interoperability. Set
LIBMPQ_ARCHIVE_CREATE_COMPRESSION_EXTENDED in the creation flags to allow
additional implemented combinations such as standalone Huffman in MPQ v2.
EXTENDED output may be less interoperable with other MPQ implementations.
Readers remain permissive and do not use this setting. Query whether a
compression selection is allowed by the writer policy with
.BR libmpq__archive_compression_allowed (3).
.PP
An archive handle is not safe for concurrent operations. Use
\fBlibmpq__archive_clone\fP() to create one independent reader per worker.
Cloning reopens the original backing path and reparses its metadata; it is
not snapshot semantics. The path must remain readable and unchanged while
clones are created or used.
